#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""channel: the showrunner's control panel for the Puddle Park channel (runs on the GPU box).

  channel status                 is everything running, is production keeping up, queue, image library, GPU/RAM
  channel recent [N]             the last N scenes written (segment, title, cast, backdrop, card)
  channel scene [NAME|last]      the full script of one scene (default: the newest)
  channel frames [N]             grab N frames from what is on air right now; prints the image paths (look at them)
  channel direct "TEXT"          give the producer a standing direction (it reads it within seconds)
  channel notes                  the standing directions, numbered
  channel unnote N               remove standing direction number N
  channel brief                  print the channel brief (the producer's bible); edit the file it names to change it
  channel library                ready backdrops and title cards, and images still being made
  channel order backdrop|card NAME "PROMPT" [--text WORDS]   order a new image from MOSS (made between blocks)
  channel logs producer|worker [N]
  channel restart producer|worker   only when one is stuck or dead

  New actions (the engineer agent builds them, the owners approve them):
  channel propose "TITLE" "WHAT IT SHOULD DO"   file a request for a new action (showrunner)
  channel proposals                             requests and their status: new, building, ready, live, rejected, failed
  channel actions                               approved plug-in actions the producer can use now
  channel submit ID FILE.py                     hand a finished, tested action in for review (engineer)
  channel approve ID | reject ID "WHY" | retire ACTION    owners only, from a root login on the box

Run as root, the commands act directly. Run as any other user (the showrunner agent), they are sent to the root-side
service (`channel serve`, a Unix socket), which is the only way that user can touch the channel.
"""
